AB  - <jats:p>The study illustrated the deterioration effects of ammonia stress on rainbow trout muscle quality (texture and flavor) and how these effects were alleviated by ascorbic acid. Ascorbic acid alleviated ammonia stress in rainbow trout by enhancing ion exchange and regulating the TLR5/NF-κB pathway, further alleviating inflammation and apoptosis, increasing the contraction degree of myofibrils by regulating the MyoD, MyoG and CAPN2, finally leading to a decrease of water-holding capacity and shear force. Ammonia detoxification was achieved through two fronts: accelerating glutamate consumption and enhancing the ornithine cycle, both of which regulated energy metabolism to provide sufficient energy. The ascorbic acid addition reduced the accumulation of 1-octene-3-alcohol, (E) -2-nonenal, lessening the earthy-moldy and fishy flavor but not completely eliminate the off-flavors. The research proposes a theoretical basis for the development of comprehensive environmental stress regulation techniques in aquaculture to improve fish health and enhance muscle flavor and texture.</jats:p>
