AB  - Salmon Aquaculture Nutrient and Metal Analysis in Rocky Benthic Communities (Bay of Fundy, Canada) This release contains the complete R-based analytical pipeline supporting the manuscript: "Salmon aquaculture-derived nutrients and metals in biota from rocky habitats in the Bay of Fundy" Journal: [To be added] | DOI: To be added upon publication Overview This repository provides a fully reproducible workflow for assessing nutrient enrichment and trace metal contamination associated with Atlantic salmon aquaculture in rocky benthic habitats in the Bay of Fundy (New Brunswick, Canada). The analysis integrates trace element concentrations and stable isotope ratios from five ecologically distinct bioindicator species to evaluate spatial patterns in exposure at varying distances from aquaculture sites. Study Design Sampling conducted across three Bay Management Areas (BMA 1, BMA 2a, BMA 3a) Paired Near (68–441 m) and Away (260–2750 m) sites relative to salmon pens Data collected in 2016 and 2017 Bio-collectors deployed in rocky bottom habitats Study Species | Species | Common Name | Tissue | |--------|------------|--------| | Mytilus edulis | Blue Mussel | Whole body / muscle | | Ciona intestinalis | Vase Tunicate | Whole body | | Homarus americanus | American Lobster | Muscle | | Myoxocephalus scorpius | Shorthorn Sculpin | Whole body / muscle | | Pholis gunnellus | Rock Gunnel | Whole body / muscle | Variables Measured Trace elements (14): Al, As, Cr, Cu, Fe, Mg, Mn, Ni, P, S, Sr, V, Zn, Hg Stable isotopes (3): δ¹³C, δ¹⁵N, δ³⁴S Note: Blue Mussel samples were not collected in 2016 (mussel analyses are 2017 only). Key Features End-to-end multivariate analysis pipeline for aquatic contaminant assessment Integration of trace element chemistry and stable isotope ecology Species-specific and year-specific analytical workflows Automated handling of outliers and structured hypothesis testing Visualization outputs including ordinations, isotope biplots, and concentration comparisons Repository Contents aquaculture_stable_isotopes.ipynb — full analysis pipeline data/README.md — dataset descriptions and access information outputs/README.md — figure descriptions Analysis Pipeline The workflow is organized into 8 sections: Setup and helper functions (ordination, PERMANOVA, plotting) Data loading and preprocessing Descriptive statistics (mean ± SD; CSV export) nMDS ordination and PERMANOVA (species × year × variable type) Multi-panel ordination figures Aquaculture feed comparison (ordination with feed reference samples) Stable isotope biplots with ellipses and feed overlay Elemental concentration boxplots (Near vs. Away comparisons) Statistical Approach Ordination Non-metric multidimensional scaling (nMDS) using Bray-Curtis dissimilarity Analyses conducted separately for: Trace elements Stable isotopes Environmental vectors fitted using envfit() Hypothesis Testing PERMANOVA (adonis2) evaluating: Location × spatial structure interactions Additive spatial effects Near vs. Away differences Pairwise PERMANOVA conducted within: BMA (by Location) Location (by BMA) Outlier Handling Outliers defined as centroid distance > 2 SD Automatically detected and removed within pipeline Affected groups: Lobster (2016 elements) Lobster (2017 isotopes) Gunnel (2016 isotopes) Feed Comparison Six aquaculture feed samples included Overlaid on ordinations and isotope biplots Used to assess shifts in tissue chemistry toward feed-derived signatures Data Availability Raw data are not included due to access restrictions. See data/README.md for full dataset descriptions and variable definitions. Reproducibility Implemented in R (≥ 4.2.0) using Jupyter notebooks with an R kernel Modular helper functions enable reproducible and extensible analyses Pipeline supports species-, year-, and variable-specific subsetting License MIT License (code only). All data remain subject to original ownership and usage restrictions. Citation Full citation and DOI will be added upon publication of the associated manuscript. Contact Samantha A. McGarrigle For questions regarding the analysis or implementation
