AB  - <jats:p>The  article  presents  the  results  of  a  study  on  the  seasonal  dynamics  of  the  hydrochemical parameters of water under a combinedwater supply system at the trout farm ―Trout Kargaly‖ (Aktobe Region, Republic of Kazakhstan). The research was conducted throughout the year, covering autumn, winter, spring, and summer periods. The main hydrochemical parameters of water were analyzed from three  sources:  an  artesian  well,  the  Kargaly  Reservoir,  and  fish-rearing  ponds.  Determination  of hydrochemical indicators was carried out in accordance with the current methodological guidelines for fisheries  water  bodies.  It  was  established  that  the  quality  of  the  water  used  meets  the  regulatory standards for reservoirs intended for fish breeding and rearing. The artesian water is characterized by a stable  chemical  composition,  optimal  pH  values,  hardness,  and  dissolved  oxygen  content,  creating favorable conditions for the  cultivation of rainbow trout (Oncorhynchus mykiss). Seasonal variations in  ammonium  and  phosphate  ion  concentrations  in  pond  water  are  associated  with  natural  biological processes,  temperature  fluctuations,  and  the  specifics  of  the  combined  water  supply  system.  The observed increases in certain parameters do not exceed established limits and have no negative impact on  the  environment.  The  results  confirm  the  environmental  safety  of  the  farm’s  operation,  the efficiency of the combined water supply system, and its importance for the sustainable development of aquaculture under continental climate conditions.</jats:p>
