AB  - The expansion of environmental legislation since the 1970s has met opposition from the salmon aquaculture industry due to the perception that it constrains growth. Yet, such regulations are also argued to foster conditions conducive to sustainable industrial growth. This study investigates how the stringency of environmental regulations, along with their compliance, influences production growth in the Atlantic salmon farming industry. Through panel data analysis covering eight major salmon-producing countries, we explore their combined effect. Our findings reveal that compliance, particularly its interaction with stringency of environmental regulations, have the potential to support sustainable industry growth. This research offers valuable insights for enhancing regulatory compliance, thereby informing more effective policy formulation and implementation in the future.
