AB  - <jats:p>The article presents the results of a study on the composition of the microbiota in rainbow trout (Oncorhynchus mykiss). The analysis was conducted using DNA sequencing of hypervariable regions of the 16S rRNA gene, The study determined the total bacterial count, identified the 20 most prevalent bacterial genera, their relative abundance in the samples, and performed taxonomic classification. A total of 43 microorganisms were detected in rainbow trout, with 7 dominant bacterial phyla identified. The identified microorganisms belong to the aquatic microbial community and fish microbiota. Some of the detected genera are associated with fish product spoilage, while others, such as certain members of the identified taxa, may exhibit potential pathogenicity and pose risks of infectious diseases.</jats:p>
