AB  - <jats:p>Purpose. Evaluation of the efficiency of a prebiotic feed additive in rainbow trout feeding.
Materials and Methods. The experiment was conducted in the conditions of the problem research laboratory "Breeding of valuable sturgeon species" and the research laboratory "Analysis of feed and livestock products" of the faculty of Biotechnology and Veterinary Medicine of the Volgograd State Agrarian University. Objects of research: rainbow trout (Oncorhynchus mykiss) and "Beta-flora" prebiotic additive containing inulin, beta-glucans, fructooligosaccharides. The control and three experimental groups of 400 heads each were formed to conduct experimental studies. Fish were fed during daylight hours. The frequency of feeding, daily norms and granule sizes were changed taking into account the water temperature, the amount of dissolved oxygen and the live weight of the fish. The feed used was EFICO Sigma 811 R compound feed. The fish in the experimental groups received "Beta-flora" prebiotic additive in addition to the compound feed, with different levels of the additive inclusion (25, 50, 75 mg / kg of feed). This additive was not used in the control group. The physicochemical parameters of water (according to OST 15.282-83), growth dynamics (according to weekly weighing data), survival, interior and hematological parameters (by cutting off the tail and taking samples from the tail vein) were assessed.
Results. The results of the studies showed that the use of the prebiotic supplement has a positive effect on the growth, survival and immunological characteristics of fish. The best results were obtained at a dosage of 75 mg / kg, where the survival rate reached 88.8%, and the weight – 15.3 g. All hematological parameters corresponded to the physiological norm, and the content of leukocytes was higher in the experimental groups.
Conclusion. The prebiotic additive can be recommended for use in the diet of rainbow trout in industrial fish farming conditions.</jats:p>
