AB  - <jats:p>This article presents the development and feasibility of a semi-industrialized process for the production 
of rainbow trout [Oncorhynchus mykiss] in Valle de Bravo, State of Mexico, through the design of a 
business plan. The plan aims to optimize rainbow trout production by implementing an industrialization 
process for this species, thereby providing a product with high nutritional value to the low-income 
population in the region and the State of Mexico. The proposal proposes the production of a trout-based 
food packed in a high vacuum, with a 75-gram serving presentation, which facilitates its transportation, 
consumption, and storage. Through the design of the business plan, a market analysis, the design and 
location of the production plant, the functional and organizational structure of the proposal, and the 
evaluation of costs and financial projections were carried out. These conclusions indicate that the 
proposed model is economically viable and has great potential to improve the nutrition of the low-income 
population by offering an affordable product with high nutritional value.</jats:p>
