AB  - Salmon farming have grown to become Norway’s second largest industry after oil totalling a turnover of 65 billion NOK in 2021 (approximately 6.5 billion euro). The industry has grown fast and is today a major political and economic power. This development is often described as a fairy tale, but the dark sides of the story are becoming ever clearer. This chapter deals with emissions from the production of salmon and tries to explain how the industry can keep on polluting the environment at such a scale.
