AB  - <jats:p>ECR Spotlight is a series of interviews with early-career authors from a selection of papers published in Journal of Experimental Biology and aims to promote not only the diversity of early-career researchers (ECRs) working in experimental biology but also the huge variety of animals and physiological systems that are essential for the ‘comparative’ approach. Wisdom Agbeti is an author on ‘ Heart rate and activity patterns of Chinook salmon (Oncorhynchus tshawytscha) under steady and unsteady flow conditions’, published in JEB. Wisdom conducted the research described in this article while a PhD student in Dr Leonardo Magnoni's lab at the Plant &amp; Food Research Institute, Nelson, New Zealand. Wisdom is now in the lab of Dr Arjan P. Palstra at Wageningen University &amp; Research, The Netherlands, investigating how salmon respond physiologically and behaviourally to unsteady flow conditions to support sustainable offshore aquaculture.</jats:p>
