AB  - This chapter focuses on the prudent use of antimicrobials guided by the ethical treatment of disease while avoiding residues, as well as minimizing environmental impacts and the risk of the development of antimicrobial resistance (AMR). It The chapter also focuses primarily on data from Atlantic salmon as they are generally available and robust in quality. Homeotherms are organisms that have the ability to maintain a relatively constant body temperature independent of their environmental temperature. Degree days is an important concept to understand in aquaculture and aquatic medicine. The approach to antimicrobial use and regulation is very highly variable across the different aquaculture-producing countries. Antimicrobial stewardship is an important concept and tool to address the development and management of AMR and to help ensure that the few treatments that exist for aquatic species remain effective.
