AB  - Panel of farmers. Camera and mic adjustments in first few seconds <br> 00:39 Anne Schwartz from Washington Tilth gives welcoming remarks <br> 02:32 Representative from Korean Farmers Association speaks through interpreter about challenges of being a farmer in Korea and impacts of WTO <br> 10:06 Jose Bove farmer from France speaks about need for farmer unity. Farmers should feed their own population not for export. Role of WTO in agricultural policies in Europe. Opposes GMO <br> 14:28 Keith Dittrich, President American Corn Growers Association explains why corn farmers are concerned about WTO decisions on agriculture. Wants every nation to be able to develop their own agricultural policies. WTO agenda will fail family farmers Proposes the creation of an international food reserve and international market share agreements for fair market prices. WTO is prioritizing multinational grain export companies <br> 19:20 Rafael Alegria Via Campesina from Honduras. Small farmers are living a tragedy in Honduras from the combination of Hurricane Mitch and humanitarian aid that dumps farm surpluses in Honduras. Also, the WTO, IMF, and World Bank that are privatizing land and water, and locking out farmers. We need to join forces to fight against the WTO. <br> Dena Hoff, Northern Plains Resource Council. Describes how Montana family farms have seen a drastic reduction in income because farm prices are set by giant agribusiness. WTO forces countries to import farm surplus from other countries. <br> 30:05 Japanese representative from Akita Prefecture Committee on Rice and Agricultural policies. Talks about food sovereignty, food dignity, and WTO <br> 38:52 Warren MacDonald, Capilano Pacific small boat fisherman. Talks about farmed salmon industry and impact on independent fisherman and on salmon <br> 42: 59 Rafael Mariano Philippine Peasant Movement KMP. GATT led to a rice import into Philippines that is over 40% of domestic rice consumption. Plus corn imports from US. Pushes down prices of local farm produce. KMP is calling on farmers around the world to strengthen solidarity ties and fight neoliberalism and take agriculture out of WTO <br> Denise O'Brien co-founder Women Food and Agriculture Network WFAN. Small farmer from Iowa. Women produce over 60% of food in the world but not at table talking about agricultural issues This item is part of the Independent Media Center World Trade Organization video recordings and log books collection at the Labor Archives of Washington, University of Washington Libraries. Laborarchives.org This item contains two parts: video file and caption tracks.
