AB  - Fish health is important in aquaculture, and early disease detection can mitigate large-scale losses. In this study, an image dataset, SalmonScan, is utilized, which is divided into two classes: fresh salmon and infected salmon. A novel model has been proposed based on CNN architectures (InceptionV3, ResNet50, DenseNet-121) with convolutional block attention module (CBAM) mechanism. Experimental results show that InceptionV3 provides a superior classification accuracy of 96.50 % on training, and 92.40 % on testing. These findings demonstrate that attention-based deep learning methods can provide an effective tool for fish health diagnosis, potentially assist farmers make timely decisions, and improve aquaculture productivity.
