AB  - <jats:p>Currently, salmon fish are in steady demand in Russia. At the same time, there is a need to expand the range of delicatessen products. Arctic char and its lake form — palia are of great interest for cold-water aquaculture. Ladoga palia, the lake form of the Arctic char, is a promising aquaculture object. For growing in cold-water farms, the Ladoga palia is most adapted, which also needs artificial reproduction to replenish the natural reserves of Lake Ladoga. The biotechnology of its reproduction has been worked out in fish farms of the Leningrad Region. However, it should be noted that palia is very demanding on the conditions of keeping and feeding, is susceptible to outbreaks of diseases such as aeromonosis and myxobacteriosis. Under the same growing conditions, palia is susceptible to infection by ichthyophthyriosis with greater intensity and estenicity than rainbow trout and Atlantic salmon. To solve the problem, it is possible to use Roncoleukin (recombinant interleukin-2) to correct immunity, which activates adaptive immunity. In 2025, experimental work was carried out in the cold-water basin farm of IP Romanov (Leningrad Region) on the use of this drug in annual Ladoga palia. Ronkoleikin was administered into the feed by irrigation at a dose of 6000 IU per kg of body weight. The course of administration was three days, the drug was administered during the first feeding. The company conducted three preventive courses, while the break between courses was 10 days. At the beginning of the experiment, the body weight of the fish in the test and control groups was 45.6±0.96 g and 45.1±0.90 g, respectively. At the end of the experiment, the average body weight of yearlings in the control reached 52.4±1.00, in the experiment — 53.0±1.30 g. By the end of the observations, an absolute increase of 7.9 g was obtained in the experimental group. This is 1.2 times higher than in the control group. At the same time, the relative growth rate was 16.1%, 1.2 times higher than the growth rate in the control. A higher content of non-specific immune complexes was detected in the experimental group of Ladoga palia, as well as a more active course of erythropoiesis and leukopoiesis. The results of experimental work make it possible to recommend an increased dosage of Ronkoleikin for Ladoga palia — 6000 IU per kg of ichthyomass.</jats:p>
