AB  - <jats:p>Currently, the priority objects for cultivation are salmon fish, they belong to the most valuable fish species, familiar to the consumer as a delicacy product with a high content of useful substances. Closed ultrasonic systems with a closed water supply device do not depend on environmental factors, which expands the geography of salmon farming in them and increases the volume of products produced by aquaculture. This article presents the results of studies on juvenile rainbow trout and juvenile trout to determine the effectiveness of a probiotic agent based on lactic acid bacteria on the safety index when growing salmon fish in a closed-type water supply system. The work was carried out at the Department of Morphology and Physiology, feeding, breeding and private Animal Husbandry of the Faculty of Veterinary Medicine and Biotechnology of the Ulyanovsk State Agrarian University, the experimental part was carried out in the Peasant farm "Dudko O.A." of the Ulyanovsk region, Cherdaklinsky district in the conditions of the private fish breeding complex "Yantarny Ruchey" - an aquaculture enterprise with a closed water supply cycle.The authors determined the effectiveness of a probiotic agent based on Pediococcus acidilactici at low water temperatures when growing cold-loving salmon fish. The positive effect of a probiotic supplement has been experimentally established when feeding juvenile salmon fish at the early stages of their growth and development. An increase in the safety and increase in the live weight of juvenile fish was revealed when growing in installations with a closed water supply cycle, It helps to increase the safety of juvenile trout by 33.8...42% and juvenile trout by 28.5%, as well as the intensity of the increase in live weight of individuals by 20.4...25 and 23%, respectively.</jats:p>
