AB  - <jats:p>Potato pink rot, caused by Phytophthora erythroseptica, is a significant soilborne disease affecting potato production. Symptoms include tuber rot with a characteristic salmon-pink discoloration when exposed to air. To evaluate the efficacy of chemicals for controlling pink rot in potatoes, a field trial was conducted in 2024 at the Aroostook Research Farm in Presque Isle, ME, using the susceptible cultivar ‘Kennebec’. This study evaluates the performance of four fungicides applied as seed and soil treatments under field conditions, providing valuable insights for improving disease management strategies for potato growers.</jats:p>
