AB  - The purpose of the study was to evaluate the effect of synbiotics containing natural minerals (zeolite and vermiculite) and the probiotic strain Escherichia coli 39SN on the indicators of natural resistance and the histomorphological structure of the organs of rainbow trout (Oncorhynchus mykiss).Three groups of fish (200 specimens each) were reared under identical conditions for 90 days.The control group received a basic diet, while the experimental groups received diets supplemented with synbiotics based on zeolite or vermiculite.Hematological and immunological analyses were carried out on day 0, 30, 60, and 90.Statistical analysis (t-test, P < 0.05) revealed that both synbiotic formulations increased erythrocyte and leukocyte counts, hemoglobin concentration, and serum protein level compared with the control.The bactericidal and phagocytic activities of blood serum were significantly higher in fish receiving synbiotics.Histological examination confirmed that the use of synbiotics did not cause any destructive or pathological changes in the internal organs, intestines, or gills of rainbow trout.The results indicate that synbiotics combining natural minerals and E. coli 39SN safely enhance the physiological and immune status of rainbow trout and can be recommended for practical use in aquaculture.
