AB  - <jats:title>Abstract</jats:title>
<jats:p><jats:italic>Caligus rogercresseyi</jats:italic> is an ectoparasitic copepod that affects salmon farms, generating negative effects on the productivity of the industry. The present study consisted of applying data science and machine learning techniques to data on <jats:italic>C. rogercresseyi</jats:italic> infection from <jats:italic>Salmo salar</jats:italic> farming centres in the Aysen region. The multiple regression models show a significant inverse relationship between total <jats:italic>C. rogercresseyi</jats:italic> infections (females, males, both adults together, and juveniles), with latitude and temperature, and a significant direct relationship with longitude and salinity for the total data. The results agree with observations for infection rates of <jats:italic>C. rogercresseyi</jats:italic> in farmed salmon in the southern part of Chile.</jats:p>
