AB  - Regulation is a legal constraint that applies to all sectors of economic activity. Products derived from blue biotechnologies and the processes used in their manufacture are no exception to this rule. Worldwide, few transgenic animals are approved for commercialization. Among genetically modified fish, AquAdvantage salmon is the only one to be produced in aquaculture for human consumption. In addition to regulatory considerations relating to the product, the FDA has also established constraints on the production of transgenic salmon. Aquatic products, whether of marine or freshwater origin, are subject in Europe and particularly in France to regulations governing traceability. The Australian and New Zealand regulations establish stricter criteria for maximum values of iodine and inorganic arsenic for edible algae than those defined in the French regulations. Countries that have traditionally included seaweed in their diet have no specific regulations governing this type of foodstuff.
