AB  - Symmorphus laoticus Gusenleitner, 2010 Figs 4 A – H, 5 A – E Symmorphus laoticus Gusenleitner, 2010: 695, 702, male – “ Laos, Phongsaly Pr., Phongsaly env., 21°41'N, 102°06'E, 1500 m ” (Oberösterreichischen Landesmuseum, Linz). Notes. Gusenleitner (2010) reported this species from Laos based on male specimens, although the abstract incorrectly refers to female. Nguyen et al. (2014) later reported the species from Vietnam for the first time based on female specimens in a checklist. Here we provide the first description of the female, based on Vietnamese material. Material examined. Vietnam • 1 ♀; Cao Bang, Tra Linh, Thang Hen lake, 22°45'47.5"N, 106°17'35.7"E, alt. 619 m, 20. v. 2023, Lien Thi Phuong Nguyen, Ngat Thi Tran, Cuong Quang Nguyen leg.; Lao Cai, Bat Xat National Reserve, Y Ty [• 6 ♀; road to Nhiu Co San mountain, salmon farm, 22°36'29.5"N, 103°37'29.6"E, alt. 1869 m, 6. v. 2019, Cuong Quang Nguyen leg. • 2 ♀; Phan Can Su, 22°38'44"N, 103°37'23"E, alt. 1800 m, 1. viii. 2019, Lien Thi Phuong Nguyen, Cuong Quang Nguyen leg. • 7 ♀ 2 ♂; Phan Can Su, 22°39'19"N, 103°37'27"E, alt. 1931 m, 1. viii. 2019, Lien Thi Phuong Nguyen et al. leg.] • 1 ♀; Lao Cai, Bat Xat, Phan Xi Pang mountain, 22°18'43"N, 103°46'00"E, alt. 2800 m, Lien Thi Phuong Nguyen, Cuong Quang Nguyen leg. • 1 ♀ 2 ♂; Lao Cai, Bat Xat, Bat Xat National Reserve, Y Ty, Phan Can Su, 22°39'19"N, 103°37'27"E, alt. 1931 m, 1. viii. 2019, Lien Thi Phuong Nguyen et al. leg. • 1 ♀ 1 ♂; Thua Thien Hue, Bach Ma National Park, way to the top, 21–26. viii. 2023, Thai Van Mai leg. • 1 ♀; Dak Lak, Krong Bong, Krong Kmar, Chu Yang Sin National Park, 12°25'18.4"N, 108°17'49.4"E, alt. 1052 m, 3. v. 2016, Lien Thi Phuong Nguyen, Dai Dac Nguyen, Ngat Thi Tran leg. [IB]. Description. Female (Fig. 4 H): Body length 10.0–11.0 mm; forewing length 10.5–11.5 mm. Male characters are in the square brackets. Head in frontal view subcircular, approximately 1.1 × as wide as high (Fig. 4 A) [1.2 × as wide as high (Fig. 4 B)]. Vertex weakly sloping posteriorly behind posterior ocelli toward occipital carina, with cephalic foveae, foveae filled with setae, distance between foveae about the distance between posterior ocelli [without cephalic fovea]. Interocular area unraised. Distance from posterior ocelli to apical margin of vertex about 2.6 × the distance from posterior ocelli to inner margin of compound eye (Fig. 4 C) [2.9 × the distance from posterior ocelli to inner margin of compound eye]. Gena in lateral view narrower than compound eye, about 0.5 × as wide as compound eye [gena about 0.7 × as wide as compound eye]; occipital carina dorsally with two submedial incisions that delimit a blunt median tooth, widen laterally. Distance between eyes at vertex approximately 1.3 × that at clypeus (Fig. 4 A) [about 2 × (Fig. 4 B)]. Clypeus in frontal view about as high as wide [about 1.3 × as high as wide]; apical margin shallowly emarginate, the emargination about 0.4 × width of clypeus between inner eye margins [apical margin deeply emarginate, the emargination about 0.6 × width of clypeus between inner compound eye margins], with two blunt teeth apically [with two sharp teeth apically]. Mandible with five prominent broad teeth [with four short teeth]. Antennal scape long, about 4.2 × as long as its maximum width [antennal scape short, about 3.5 × as its maximum width]; flagellomere I about 1.3 × as long as wide [about 2.1 × as long as wide], flagellomere II as wide as long, flagellomeres III – IV longer than wide, flagellomere V – IX wider than long, flagellomere X bullet shape, as long as wide. Propodeum with a large deep fovea behind metanotum, and a strong carina running from the fovea to apical margin, posterior face with oblique weak carina, and rugose laterally (Fig. 4 E). Tergum I with a shallow longitudinal furrow and a transverse carina basally (Fig. 4 F). Tergum II and sternum II in lateral view angle near base (Fig. 4 G). Sculpturing. Similar to the male, except that the clypeus with larger and stronger punctures. Color. Body black. Yellow markings present as follows: two small spots near base of clypeus, a spot between antennal socket, two small spots at vertex behind compound eyes, an apical transverse band at apical margin of tergum I, and near apical margin of tergum II, a small spot on dorsal part of mesepisternum. Genitalia. Male genitalia were examined from specimen collected in Lao Cai province, Vietnam (1 ♂; Lao Cai, Bat Xat, Bat Xat National Reserve, Y Ty, Phan Can Su, 22°39'19"N, 103°37'27"E, alt. 1931 m, 1. viii. 2019, Lien Thi Phuong Nguyen et al. leg.) (Fig. 5 A – E). Metasomal sternum VIII slightly greater than 2.3 × as long as wide, with basal margin slightly convex (Fig. 5 A). Parameral spine without setae. Volsella flattened and spatulate, widened on inner margin, without apical setae (Fig. 5 B). Digitus parallel-sided from near base to basal one-third, then narrowing to apex, with rounded apex (Fig. 5 C), slightly more than 2 × as long as wide; surface sparsely covered with medium setae. Penis valve short, about 1.3 × as long as basal apodeme (Fig. 5 D); in profile, apical part strongly produced laterally to form a blunt projection (Fig. 5 E). Distribution. Laos; Vietnam.
