AB  - Salmon Mortality Monitor is an R Shiny application developed by the Centre for Epidemiology and Planetary Health (CEPH), SRUC, as part of the DECIDE project. It turns routine mortality records into interactive summaries, time trends, and cause breakdowns, supporting two views: an industry-wide overview and per-site comparisons against the industry benchmark. The aim is to make farmed-salmon mortality data easier to explore and interpret — for individual sites tracking their own performance, and for understanding patterns across the wider industry.
