AB  - <jats:p>Bacterial kidney disease (BKD, Dee's disease) – the causative agent of which is the gram–positive nonsporous immobile bacterium Renibacterium salmoninarum – is a common disease of salmon fish (Salmonidae), which causes significant damage to fish production in aquaculture and the development of the industry, as well as reduces the number of wild populations. The article shows the result of morphological and ultrastructural characteristics of R. salmoninarum (strain KIM-16) obtained in the Northwestern region of the Russian Federation. In this study, specific organelles called microvesicles were discovered.</jats:p>
