AB  - <jats:p>Ladoga palia — the lake form of the Arctic char, needs artificial reproduction to replenish the reserves of the natural population of Lake Ladoga. It is a promising aquaculture, for commercial production and recreational fishing. It has a spectacular appearance and excellent taste. Palia is extremely demanding on the conditions of keeping, feeding and well as more sensitive to bacterial and parasitic diseases than other salmon fish. Even under optimal conditions of the cold-water basin economy, a deterioration
in the epizootic state and a decrease in immunity and physiological status are possible. Studies conducted on rainbow trout and Atlantic salmon have shown that the solution to the problem is possible when using Roncoleikin. In 2024, in the cold-water basin economy of IP Romanov (Leningrad Region), studies were carried out on the use of this drug in annual Ladoga palia. Roncoleukin was administered orally with feed by irrigation at a dose of 6000 IU per kg of body weight for three days in the first feeding. 2 courses of preventive feeding were carried out sequentially, the break between courses was 10 days. The average body weight in the control was initially 13.6±0.41 g, in the experiment — 14.0±0.43 g. At the end of the experiment, the average body weight in the control reached 19.0±0.50 g, in the experiment — 22.0±0.48 g (p ≤ 0.001). At the same time, the achieved effect remained for a month after the completion of the course of the drug. By the end of the observations in the experimental group, the absolute growth is 1.7 times higher than in the control, and the relative growth rate is 1.4. In the
leukogram of experimental fish revealed the absence of eosinophils and basophils which indicates the absence of an inflammatory process in the body and a better physiological state. This makes it possible to recommend an increased dosage of 6000 IU per kg of body weight for use as Ladoga palia.</jats:p>
